TY  - RPRT
TI  - Precision Clinical Renal Nutrition & Medication Safety in Maintenance Hemodialysis: A Scoping Synthesis of KDOQI 2020, KDIGO 2024, Phosphorus Bioavailability, and Transplant CYP3A4 Guardrails
AU  - White, Andre
AU  - NorthStar Collaborative Research Faculty
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026/10/21
PB  - NorthStar Prime Research & Publishing Institute
AB  - Synthesizing 53 clinical trials and nephrology practice guidelines (KDOQI 2020, ADA 2026 Section 11, KDIGO 2024, CONVINCE, PIVOTAL), this scoping review formalizes six computational and clinical guardrails for maintenance hemodialysis (CKD Stage 5D) nutrition informatics: (1) preserving 1.0-1.2 g/kg/day high-biological-value protein to prevent protein-energy wasting (PEW); (2) stratifying dietary phosphorus by gastrointestinal bioavailability (20%-40% plant phytate < 40%-60% animal organic < 90%-100% inorganic 'phos' additives; Kalantar-Zadeh et al., CJASN, 2010); (3) enforcing a strict 'Missing != Zero' database integrity rule for undeclared phosphorus in USDA Branded Foods; (4) accounting for culinary potassium-leaching heterogeneity (Martinez-Pineda et al., 2020; Batista et al., 2021) and prohibiting KCl salt substitutes; (5) USDA safe minimum internal cooking temperatures (145°F fish / 165°F poultry); and (6) excluding cannabinoids (THC/CBD) from renal culinary programs because their pharmacokinetics in advanced CKD are poorly studied, they are not expected to be meaningfully removed by dialysis (high protein binding), and cannabidiol (CBD) increased tacrolimus exposure 3.1-fold (AUC) and 4.2-fold (Cmax) in a Phase I trial (Clin Pharmacol Ther 2025; PMID 39601108; doi:10.1002/cpt.3504).
